THOUGHT: NullAway still thinks `newDrawableResource` can return null because `LazyBitmapDrawableResource.obtain` is annotated `@Nullable`. However, at this call site we know the argument is non-null, so the result is non-null. To satisfy NullAway without changing `LazyBitmapDrawableResource`, I’ll add an explicit null check and throw if it ever is null, then return the non-null value. This preserves behavior (it should never happen) and gives NullAway a clear guarantee. Then I’ll rebuild to confirm the specific error is gone and no new ones are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/glide && sed -i '75,79c\  private Resource<Drawable> newDrawableResource(Context context, Resource<Bitmap> transformed) {
    Resource<? extends Drawable> result =
        LazyBitmapDrawableResource.obtain(context.getResources(), transformed);
    if (result == null) {
      throw new IllegalStateException("Unable to obtain Drawable Resource from Bitmap");
    }
    return (Resource<Drawable>) result;
  }' library/src/main/java/com/bumptech/glide/load/resource/bitmap/DrawableTransformation.java && ./gradlew library:compileDebugJavaWithJavac -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "DrawableTransformation.java" new_build_output.log || tail -n 60 new_build_output.log
```

